  (range 18-56) participated in the study. The leakage index was a five point scale (1 = never, 5 = always) containing  
  thirteen types of physical exertions known to trigger urinary leakage. The social activity index contains nine        
  social settings in which women may have problems to participate. For each parameter a 10 cm visual analogue scale (0  
  = impossible to participate, 10 = no problem to participate) was used for registration. The correlation coefficient   
  for test 1 and 2 was .92 (p < 0.01) and .94 (p < 0.01) for the leakage and the social activity index, respectively.   
